  "raw_text": "The user wants me to solve a word problem involving sharing the cost of a pizza.\nProblem statement:\nSeven students shared the cost of a $\\$26.00$ pizza.\nEach student paid either $\\$3.71$ or $\\$3.72$.\nI need to find how many students paid $\\$3.72$.\n\nLet $x$ be the number of students who paid $\\$3.71$.\nLet $y$ be the number of students who paid $\\$3.72$.\n\nWe know there are 7 students in total, so:\n$x + y = 7$  (Equation 1)\n\nWe also know the total cost is $\\$26.00$. So:\n$3.71x + 3.72y = 26.00$  (Equation 2)\n\nI need to solve for $y$.\n\nMethod 1: Substitution.\nFrom Equation 1, $x = 7 - y$.\nSubstitute into Equation 2:\n$3.71(7 - y) + 3.72y = 26.00$\n$3.71 \\times 7 - 3.71y + 3.72y = 26.00$\nCalculate $3.71 \\times 7$:\n$3.71 \\times 7 = 25.97$\nSo, $25.97 - 3.71y + 3.72y = 26.00$\nCombine like terms ($-3.71y + 3.72y = 0.01y$):\n$25.97 + 0.01y = 26.00$\nSubtract $25.97$ from both sides:\n$0.01y = 26.00 - 25.97$\n$0.01y = 0.03$\nDivide by $0.01$:\n$y = 3$\n\nSo, 3 students paid $\\$3.72$.\nLet's check $x$.\n$x = 7 - 3 = 4$.\nCheck total cost:\n$4 \\times 3.71 + 3 \\times 3.72$\n$= 14.84 + 11.16$\n$= 26.00$\nThis works.\n\nMethod 2: Difference approach.\nThe difference in payment per person is $3.72 - 3.71 = 0.01$.\nIf everyone paid $\\$3.71$, the total would be $7 \\times 3.71 = 25.97$.\nThe actual total is $\\$26.00$.\nThe difference is $26.00 - 25.97 = 0.03$.\nSince each student switching from paying $\\$3.71$ to paying $\\$3.72$ adds $\\$0.01$ to the total, we need to find how many such switches add up to $\\$0.03$.\nNumber of students paying $\\$3.72 = \\frac{0.03}{0.01} = 3$.\n\nBoth methods yield the same result. I will write down the solution using the steps structure requested.\n\nStructure constraints:\n- Native thinking block.\n- Math reasoning inside must consist only of consecutive numbered sections.\n- Begin immediately with Step 1: followed by mathematical work.\n- Start each later section on a new line as Step 2:, Step 